import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Persist A2A artifacts as verifiable facts."
  description="Configure StateKnot's immutable PostgreSQL artifact registry, private S3-compatible bytes, direct task polling, authorization-first reads, and integrity verification."
  section="Durable artifact storage"
>
  <aside class="docs-callout" aria-labelledby="artifact-boundary-title">
    <h2 id="artifact-boundary-title">Implemented pre-alpha boundary</h2>
    <p>
      Terminal A2A task parts can now become tenant-qualified <code
        >ArtifactRef</code
      > values instead of inline Tool JSON. Migration 18 stores immutable metadata;
      a private S3-compatible backend stores bytes. The API remains unstable, and
      general retention, registry-aware orphan collection, public downloads, signed
      artifacts, and live-provider qualification are not shipped.
    </p>
  </aside>

  <section aria-labelledby="artifact-flow-title">
    <h2 id="artifact-flow-title">Follow one evidence chain</h2>
    <div class="docs-code" data-code-block>
      <div class="docs-code-head">
        <span>Durable A2A completion</span>
        <button
          class="copy-button affordance"
          type="button"
          data-copy-button
          data-copy-target="artifact-flow-code"
        >
          <span data-copy-label aria-live="polite">Copy</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <pre
        id="artifact-flow-code"
        tabindex="0"><code>Executing event → one A2A send → task recovery handle
  → direct GetTask polling (no business resend)
  → bounded terminal parts → unique staging object
  → conditional-create final object → length + SHA-256 verification
  → immutable PostgreSQL registration → authorized verified read</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p>
      The final key is deterministic for the exact tenant, run, logical
      invocation, physical attempt, origin event, Tool, remote identities, and
      part position. Exact retries converge. An existing object with different
      bytes is an integrity failure, never an overwrite opportunity.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="artifact-invariants-title">
    <h2 id="artifact-invariants-title">
      Keep metadata, bytes, and authority separate
    </h2>
    <dl class="docs-definition-list">
      <div>
        <dt>Private bytes</dt>
        <dd>
          Startup performs a real put, conditional copy, read, repeated-copy
          rejection, and delete probe. A backend that cannot prove immutable
          final publication is rejected before traffic.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Immutable registry</dt>
        <dd>
          PostgreSQL binds canonical reference bytes and digest, content length
          and digest, origin run/event, same-tenant parents, idempotency key,
          and a private locator. Object I/O never runs inside its transaction.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Authorization first</dt>
        <dd>
          The exact principal and tenant-qualified identity are authorized
          before registry lookup, preventing existence or locator disclosure.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Verified resolution</dt>
        <dd>
          Captured version/ETag preconditions are applied when available.
          Complete length and SHA-256 verification finishes before any byte is
          returned.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="artifact-config-title">
    <h2 id="artifact-config-title">
      Build and probe the exact production backend
    </h2>
    <div class="docs-code" data-code-block>
      <div class="docs-code-head">
        <span>Rust · current pre-alpha API</span>
        <button
          class="copy-button affordance"
          type="button"
          data-copy-button
          data-copy-target="artifact-config-code"
        >
          <span data-copy-label aria-live="polite">Copy</span>
        </button>
      </div>
      <pre
        id="artifact-config-code"
        tabindex="0"><code>let objects = S3CompatibleBackendBuilder::from_env(bucket, region)?
    .with_https_endpoint(endpoint)?
    .with_conditional_copy(S3ConditionalCopy::AmazonMultipart)
    .with_sha256_checksum()
    .with_kms_key_id(kms_key)?
    .build()?;

let artifacts = Arc::new(StateKnotArtifactStore::initialize(
    objects,
    Arc::new(postgres_store.clone()),
    Arc::new(read_authorizer),
    "production-artifacts-v1",
    options,
).await?);

let remote = A2aRemoteAgent::bind_with_durable_artifacts(
    descriptor, client, "answer", delivery, recovery, schemas, artifacts,
)?;</code></pre>
    </div>
    <p>
      AWS S3 uses the multipart conditional-copy strategy. Other compatible
      providers may require a documented destination-precondition header and
      status. Test the exact endpoint, bucket policy, encryption policy, and
      workload identity; do not infer atomic behavior from an S3-compatible
      label.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>from_env</code> imports only credential-selection variables. Environment
      endpoints, HTTP enablement, metadata overrides, unsigned requests, retry behavior,
      bucket/region selection, and encryption settings cannot bypass this builder.
      Configure a non-default web-identity STS endpoint explicitly through <code
        >with_https_sts_endpoint</code
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="artifact-egress-title">
    <h2 id="artifact-egress-title">
      Treat URL parts as a separate egress boundary
    </h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Allow only exact production HTTPS origins with explicit IP pins.</li>
      <li>
        Revalidate every redirect hop; reject URL credentials and fragments.
      </li>
      <li>
        Disable environment proxies, implicit retries, cookies, automatic
        redirects, and transparent content decoding.
      </li>
      <li>
        Require identity encoding, consistent media types, and bounded declared
        and observed lengths.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Literal loopback HTTP is reserved for tests or a managed same-host
      sidecar. Tool limits further bound artifact count, total bytes, each part,
      and the completion projection.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="artifact-limits-title">
    <h2 id="artifact-limits-title">
      Bound resources and operate cleanup explicitly
    </h2>
    <div class="docs-table-wrap" tabindex="0">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Limit</th><th>Default</th><th>Hard ceiling</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Object operation</td><td>60 s</td><td>10 min</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Complete remote request</td><td>120 s</td><td>10 min</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Multipart part</td><td>8 MiB</td><td>5–64 MiB</td></tr>
          <tr
            ><td>Remote object / resolved read</td><td>64 MiB</td><td>1 GiB</td
            ></tr
          >
          <tr><td>Redirects</td><td>3</td><td>3</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Concurrent operations</td><td>8</td><td>256</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p>
      One process-local permit covers each complete ingest or materialized-read
      path. Configure lifecycle rules for abandoned multipart uploads and <code
        >stateknot/staging/v1/</code
      >. Alert whenever <code>staging_cleanup_failures()</code> increases. Never apply
      a blind age rule to final objects: until registry-aware collection ships, reconcile
      suspected orphans against PostgreSQL before deletion.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="artifact-proof-title">
    <h2 id="artifact-proof-title">Know what the evidence proves</h2>
    <p>
      Tests cover exact retries, tampering, authorization-before-lookup, URL
      policy, multipart ingestion, full reads, real PostgreSQL registration,
      migration 17→18, and no-resend terminal-task recovery over both HTTP+JSON
      and JSON-RPC. Read the <a
        href="https://github.com/StateKnot/StateKnot/blob/main/docs/artifact-storage.md"
        >complete deployment and verification guide</a
      > before enabling the boundary.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
